---
import SubpageLayout from '../layouts/SubpageLayout.astro';
import Checklist from '../components/Checklist.astro';
import PhotoCredit from '../components/PhotoCredit.astro';
---
<SubpageLayout
  title="Lake View Park Islamabad Family Visit Guide"
  description="Lake View Park Islamabad family visit guide: kids’ facilities, restrooms, food, safe lake time and a comfortable visit length for parents."
  path="/family-guide/"
  faq={[
    { q: 'Why is Lake View Park good for families?', a: 'Open lawns and lakeside paths let children move freely, while play areas and boating (when operating) add structured fun. The lake is a calm backdrop rather than a busy attraction.' },
    { q: 'Are kids’ facilities and restrooms reliable?', a: 'Children’s play equipment is run by on-site operators and can change, so check what is open on the day. Ask management for the currently open restroom and its route.' },
    { q: 'How long should a family visit be?', a: 'About 2–3 hours covers a relaxed walk and play; allow half a day if you add a picnic or several activities. Keep the route short, shaded and close to restrooms for younger children.' },
    { q: 'How do we stay safe near the lake?', a: 'Supervise children near the water at all times, and only use managed boating when it is open with provided safety gear. The non-functional aviary is not a kids’ activity to plan around.' },
  ]}
  breadcrumb={[{ name: 'Home', href: '/' }, { name: 'Family guide', href: '/family-guide/' }]}
  image="/images/rawal-lake-islamabad-view.jpg"
  related={[
    { label: 'Kids play areas', href: '/kids-play-areas/' },
    { label: 'Picnic guide', href: '/picnic-guide/' },
    { label: 'Visitor facilities', href: '/visitor-facilities/' },
    { label: 'Things to do', href: '/things-to-do/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="space-y-8">
    <p class="text-lg leading-8 text-slate-700">Lake View Park is one of Islamabad’s most-visited family destinations because it combines open space, a lake and activities. This guide focuses on what parents actually need to know.</p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Why it suits families</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">Open lawns and lakeside paths let children move freely, while play areas and boating (when operating) add structured fun. The lake itself is the calm backdrop rather than a busy attraction.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Kids’ facilities and restrooms</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">Children’s play equipment is run by on-site operators and can change; check what is open on the day (see <a class="font-semibold text-[#a66f2d] underline" href="/kids-play-areas/">kids play areas</a>). Ask management for the currently open restroom and its route.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Food and a comfortable length</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">On-site food stalls and your own picnic both work. About <strong>2–3 hours</strong> covers a relaxed walk and play; allow half a day if you add a picnic or multiple activities. Keep the route short, shaded and close to restrooms for younger children.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Water safety</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">Supervise children near the lake at all times, and only use managed boating when it is open with provided safety gear. The non-functional aviary is not a kids’ activity to plan around.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-[#143844]">Keep it simple for parents</h2>
      <p class="mt-3 leading-8">The most relaxed family visit leads with open space, a short shaded route and a restroom nearby. Treat boating and rides as confirm-on-site extras, and watch children closely near the water at all times.</p>
    </section>

    <Checklist title="Family visit checklist" items={[
      'Check which play areas are open on the day.',
      'Ask management for the nearest open restroom.',
      'Plan 2–3 hours, or half a day with a picnic.',
      'Supervise children near the lake; no swimming.',
    ]} />

    <figure>
      <img src="/images/rawal-lake-islamabad-view.jpg" width="1440" height="960" alt="Lakeside structure at Rawal Lake near Lake View Park, Islamabad" class="h-[360px] w-full rounded-[2rem] object-cover card-shadow" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption><PhotoCredit photo={3} /></figcaption>
    </figure>
  </article>
</SubpageLayout>
